id: pm-vcs-tjnr
title: Install the pinned release npm into a job-local prefix
description: "The release workflow replaces the runner's global npm with the pinned npm. Parallel jobs on one runner host share the toolcache Node installation, so one job's global install mutates a sibling job's npm mid-install (ENOTEMPTY, or npm: command not found). Tracked by unbraind/pm-ops#284."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ops#284"
created_at: "2026-11-16T14:39:25.582Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T07:54:37.461Z"
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: "The release workflow installs the pinned npm with --prefix into a job-local directory and prepends that prefix bin to the job path; The workflow keeps the exact-version assertion on the effective npm; A workflow-contract test fails if any workflow replaces the global npm; Gates pass: typecheck, lint, tests, changelog:check"
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T15:18:05.935Z",codex-sol,"Continuation: verified the existing worktree and remote branch state, preserved the earlier changes, and reused this item. Rerunning required gates to completion under the continuation author before committing results."
  "2026-11-16T15:28:55.474Z",codex-sol,"Root cause confirmed in the workflow source: global installation of the pinned npm replaces the same Node installation used by parallel jobs on a shared toolcache. Replaced each bootstrap with a job-local prefix, published only its bin directory to the job PATH, and retained exact-pin checks including a separate subsequent-step assertion. Workflow contracts reject global npm replacement across all workflow files. No runner settings or shared tool installations were modified."
  "2026-11-16T15:42:42.194Z",codex-sol,The first combined gate command hit its 20-minute timeout during shared-host disk contention and is not pass evidence. Retrying all gates to completion using memory-backed temporary fixtures and the existing harness deadline scale. Assertions and test selection are unchanged.
  "2026-11-16T15:59:12.342Z",codex-sol,"Gate results before publication: typecheck and lint completed successfully; node --test test/release-approval.test.ts and changelog:check passed together. The first npm test command timed out during disk contention; the full replacement run is active and remains pending evidence. Regenerated the required self-host bundle using the repository writer. Publishing a draft for exact-head CI validation."
  "2026-11-16T16:09:19.061Z",codex-sol,"Implementation commit 139bd057e9477e86251542deaf86e18a64f31be9 installs and verifies the release npm privately to each job. Typecheck, lint, workflow contracts and changelog checks passed. The first broad npm test attempt timed out; the full replacement remains active. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification and exact-head CI."
  "2026-11-16T16:47:57.335Z",codex-sol,"The broad local npm test retry reached its 60-minute command limit during the release suite and is not pass evidence. Typecheck, lint, workflow contracts, changelog:check and the committed self-host verification passed separately. Full release-suite and hosted Windows acceptance remain pending CI. Tracking PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/213. The PR remains open for orchestrator verification; exact-head CI is queued or running."
  "2026-11-16T19:23:57.341Z",codex-sol,"Review round P: replace the workflow-wide regex with a dependency-free shell command parser and regression fixtures. Parse run scripts with existing yaml where available; preserve allowed prefix-local installs. Verify typecheck, lint or docstring, focused guard/workflow contracts and changelog checks before pushing. No review-thread actions."
  "2026-11-16T19:28:37.078Z",codex-sol,"Review round P addresses PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64FalA: shared-npm replacement guard now tokenizes shell commands and uses existing yaml for run scripts. Added 38 fixtures covering npm aliases, flag placement/location, package specs, continuations, quotes/paths, separators and allowed installs. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint and npm run changelog:check PASS. The new linked guard and workflow contracts passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress: 71 pass, 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo. Full-suite certification is left to CI; review threads remain untouched. Stage the new files and final tracker pair before self-host:write; accept:self-host must pass at committed HEAD before push."
  "2026-11-17T07:50:21.871Z",pi-guard-1117aj,"Round AJ: merged origin/main (kept both sides; the selfhost bundle is a regenerated artifact and is rewritten by the self-host gate at HEAD; no history lines rewritten), then replaced the guard's shell parser with a line-based fail-closed rule identical to the other fleet repositories: logical lines only (continuations joined, newline-only splits), comment and here-document text scanned like any other text, install family extended with update/up/upgrade/udpate, markers covering single-dash g clusters, global-containing tokens, -L with any value and two-plus-letter prefixes of global/location, npm config set/set as a run-wide global signal (narrowed to a set token: a read-only 'npm config get globalconfig' line tripped the broader form), operands naming npm by substring or computed form (tarball URLs, x@npm:npm), exemptions restricted to exact approved bootstrap lines, and step-level rejection of GITHUB_ENV npm_config_* writes and global/location npmrc writes. The accepted npx fixture moved to rejected (thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64II4P): the rule scans quoted text, so npx-prefixed and echoed global installs can no longer hide. Both guard and release-approval test files now import the session isolation helper first (thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64GMoi), and the release-approval test also asserts the bootstrap appends the same prefix's node_modules/.bin to $GITHUB_PATH and that the Verify job-local npm version step expects exactly the installed version."
  "2026-11-17T07:53:55.259Z",pi-guard-1117aj,"Gates at HEAD: guard fixtures (130) and release-approval tests pass; typecheck, eslint, duplication gate and changelog:check pass; the test-environment isolation audit passes with the corrected import order. Self-host gate executed in order: commit 0421d29, build, self-host:write, bundle commit d3c0d5d, then accept:self-host at HEAD reported the committed bundle's tip tree byte-identical to the committed source (validated external action revisions excepted). Full suite and hosted acceptance remain with CI."
